# Database (SQLite via sql.js)

- Schema definitions live in `src/schema/index.ts`.
- Repository functions live in `src/repositories/`, one file per entity (`record.ts`, `vehicles.ts`, `materials.ts`, `settings.ts`, `health.ts`).
- Interact with the DB ONLY through repository functions. Do not write inline queries outside the repository layer.

## Migrations

- Generate migrations with `drizzle-kit generate`; store them in the `drizzle/` folder (outside `src`).
- `migrate.ts` applies migrations to the development database.
- Migrations run automatically on app startup in production.

## Persistence & integrity

- With sql.js, always call `db.save()` after every mutation to persist to disk (this becomes automatic if we move to better-sqlite3).
- The `settings` table is a fixed-column table with exactly one row (`id = 1`). There is no key-value table.
- Foreign keys are used (`vehicleId`, `materialId` in `records`). Never hard-delete a vehicle/material that is referenced; restrict or soft-delete.

```ts
// GOOD - mutate via repository, then persist
const record = createRecord(db, data);
db.save();
```
